  journal     = "bioRxiv",
  institution = "bioRxiv",
  abstract    = "We make sense of everyday events by reasoning about their
                 underlying causes. When we connect causal links between events
                 separated in time, we often experience a sudden feeling of
                 ``aha!'', or a moment of insight. What cognitive and neural
                 processes underlie these moments of understanding? We
                 hypothesized that narrative insight accompanies retrieving
                 causally related past events in memory and updating the current
                 event representation. To test this, we designed an fMRI study
