  journal  = "bioRxivorg",
  abstract = "Navigating everyday environments requires that the brain perform
              information processing at multiple different timescales. For
              example, while watching a movie we use sensory information from
              every video frame to construct the current movie scene, which
              itself is continuously integrated into the narrative arc of the
