  volume    =  113,
  number    =  11,
  pages     = "1694--1707.e1",
  abstract  = "Classical models of memory in psychology and neuroscience rely on
               similarity-based retrieval of stored patterns, where similarity
               is a function of retrieval cues and the stored patterns. Although
               parsimonious, these models do not allow distinct representations
               for storage and retrieval, despite their distinct computational
