                   simple next-token predictors, such as linear networks and
                   shallow Multi-Layer Perceptrons (MLPs), display non-trivial
                   performance on text generation and arithmetic tasks. Our
                   results demonstrate that the power of today's LLMs can be
                   attributed, to a great extent, to the auto-regressive
                   next-token training scheme, and not necessarily to a
                   particular choice of architecture.",
  month         =  sep,
  year          =  2023,
  archivePrefix = "arXiv",
